From: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:41:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ramips: mt7620, mt76x8: load the kernel at 0x80008000

The 24K EPC erratum corrupts EPC[31:28] for a J or JAL located in the
first 32 KiB of a 256 MiB segment. Link and load the kernel at
0x80008000 so it has no code there, instead of padding the image from
0x80000000.

Platform: link address for SOC_MT7620 (which also covers MT7628).
Kconfig: SOC_MT7620 selects NO_EXCEPT_FILL, so head.S drops the 0x400
bytes of exception space: the kernel no longer starts at 0x80000000 and
the exception vectors are moved (SOC_MT7620 always selects
CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI).

The memory below the kernel is no longer part of the image and goes to
the page allocator; module code must not use it (see 301-02).

Signed-off-by: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
---
 arch/mips/ralink/Kconfig           | 1 +
 arch/mips/ralink/Platform          | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/mips/ralink/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/ralink/Kconfig
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ choice
 	config SOC_MT7620
 		bool "MT7620/8"
 		select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI
+		select NO_EXCEPT_FILL
 		select HAVE_PCI
 		select SOC_BUS
 
--- a/arch/mips/ralink/Platform
+++ b/arch/mips/ralink/Platform
@@ -22,9 +22,11 @@ load-$(CONFIG_SOC_RT3883)	+= 0xffffffff8
 cflags-$(CONFIG_SOC_RT3883)	+= -I$(srctree)/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ralink/rt3883
 
 #
-# Ralink MT7620
+# Ralink MT7620 (also MT7628)
 #
-load-$(CONFIG_SOC_MT7620)	+= 0xffffffff80000000
+# Link the kernel above the first 32 KiB of KSEG0: the 24K EPC erratum
+# breaks J/JAL located there (see arch/mips/kernel/module.c).
+load-$(CONFIG_SOC_MT7620)	+= 0xffffffff80008000
 cflags-$(CONFIG_SOC_MT7620)	+= -I$(srctree)/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ralink/mt7620
 
 # Ralink MT7621
